- **Fonts:** Nunito throughout student screens, including display text.
- **Radius:** ~16px controls; every bounded student shape is rounded.

## Canonical screen recipe (auth — keep this)

Reuse these classes / structure when building similar flows:

1. `.auth-hero` — soft lime band, full-width on mobile and a distinct side area on desktop
2. `.mascot` (+ idle bounce) — our owl, not Duo
3. `.speech` — one short kid line in a white bubble
4. `.brand-pill` — tiny green chip (“Học từ vựng” / step label)
5. `.field` with **2px border + `0 3px 0` ledge** (focus → green ledge)
6. Primary `.btn` ledge CTA; playful sentence-case (“Vào học thôi”)
7. `.auth-switch` footer link in `--info`

## Layout

- Mobile: compact, single-column, touch-first. Tablet: wider single-column layout.
- Desktop ≥1024px: full-width unframed student layout with sensible content bounds. Auth, path, unit, report, and games may reorganize into columns while preserving DOM order and behavior.
- At 1920×1080, a typical game question and its primary action should fit together. Use discrete larger type and targets at large breakpoints, not viewport-width font scaling. Allow scrolling on shorter screens; never clip feedback or controls.

## Do / don’t

```text
✅ Hero band + mascot + speech on entry screens
✅ Chunky green CTA + matching field ledges
✅ Brand pill + short lede
✅ Wide desktop compositions with readable classroom-sized game elements
❌ Flat thin inputs next to a 3D button
❌ Phone-sized desktop shell, decorative stage, or tiny controls on a TV
❌ Copy Duo / purple AI gradients / hearts / paywalls
❌ Redesign path/play “while touching auth” unless asked
```

